# How to capture:
#   1. Open Wireshark, filter: "tls.handshake.type == 1"
#   2. Open Safari 18, navigate to https://example.com/api/all
#   3. Right-click the ClientHello packet → Copy → "...as Hex Stream"
#   4. Paste the hex bytes below (whitespace and comments are ignored)
#
# TODO: Replace this placeholder with actual captured hex bytes.
# The hex should start with "16 03 01" (TLS Record Header).
#
# Key Safari differences vs Chrome:
#   - No GREASE in cipher suites (only in extensions)
#   - Different extension order
#   - No compress_certificate extension
#   - No ALPS extension
